Because of how important I consider reflection and MR, I usually
spend my enchant armor scrolls on all of my armor other than my
body armor until I get one of the dragon colors I want.  And AC
point is an AC point when you're counting totals, so it doesn't
matter if a point gets added to your teeshirt or your mail.  It
doesn't matter until you eventually switch to some other item
that is.

When I have a ?oEA I consider whether any of my current armor
items will still be with me at the end.  If so I will spend that
scroll on that item.  I may end up with a blessed fireproof +5
teeshirt before I encounter enough grey/silver dragons to get the
scales I want.

In the end, if I think ?oEA are plentifull I will "waste" them
on dragon scales other than grey/silver, but if I think they are
rare I will only use them on important armor like speed boots,
dexterity/power gloves, tee/hawiian-shirt, good cloaks at first.

